---
apiVersion: kuttl.dev/v1beta1
kind: TestAssert
# Terminal: the 3->2 drain finished and the gate released the decrement. Everything here is a resource
# stanza (kuttl polls silently — no per-retry command echo), which works because this is a deterministic
# spike: the AgentRequest names are predictable (gen = the Scaler's metadata.generation at this scale;
# create=1, step30=2, step50=3). Reaching Scaler `idle` requires BOTH gated steps to have reported Done.
# progress.total is 0 at Done (build_plan re-derives: once the partitions are moved off, nothing is
# "moving"), so only remaining: 0 is asserted.
timeout: 900
---
# The drain AgentRequest completed (remaining 0).
apiVersion: platform.stackable.tech/v1alpha1
kind: AgentRequest
metadata:
  name: test-kafka-broker-default-scaler-scaledown-gen3
status:
  phase: done
  progress:
    remaining: 0
---
# The PostScaling unregister ran and reached Done (agent writes Done only after UnregisterBroker
# succeeded → the removed broker's stale registration was cleaned out of the cluster metadata).
apiVersion: platform.stackable.tech/v1alpha1
kind: AgentRequest
metadata:
  name: test-kafka-broker-default-scaler-unregister-gen3
status:
  phase: done
---
# Scaler settled back to idle at 2.
apiVersion: autoscaling.stackable.tech/v1alpha1
kind: Scaler
metadata:
  name: test-kafka-broker-default-scaler
status:
  replicas: 2
  state:
    idle: {}
---
# The broker STS shrank to 2 — only because reconcile_scaler wrote replicas=2 AFTER the drain reported
# Done, so a healthy 2/2 is the k8s-level proxy that the drain completed first.
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: StatefulSet
metadata:
  name: test-kafka-broker-default
status:
  readyReplicas: 2
  replicas: 2
